{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in today because your right leg amputation stump isn’t healing well?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:32:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. The wound has this dark scab on it, and it just hasn’t been getting better. My doctor in clinic debrided a little bit today and said I needed to be admitted for more work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And how’s the pain? Are you managing okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:34:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The pain in the stump is under control with my meds, but I still have that same burning pain in my left toes. It hasn’t changed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:35:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. We’ll take a close look at both. I also see you’re on warfarin for your mechanical heart valve. Your INR came back at 4.3 today—higher than we’d like for surgery. So we’ll hold your warfarin for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:36:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, is that dangerous? The INR being high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:37:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It increases bleeding risk, especially with surgery. That’s why we’re pausing it temporarily. We’ll monitor it closely and restart when it’s safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:38:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And what about the surgery? When will that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:39:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re scheduled for tomorrow morning. We’ll remove the dead tissue from the stump and place a special vacuum dressing to help it heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:41:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The VAC again? I had that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:42:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it helps pull fluid out and encourages new tissue growth. We’ll change it every few days while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:43:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And my dialysis? I’m due tomorrow afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:44:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve scheduled it for after your surgery. You’ll have it the day after, on the 31st. We’ll remove about 1.5 liters of fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:46:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Sometimes I feel nauseous after dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2159-07-29 12:47:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll watch for that. If it happens, we can give you medication to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2159-07-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re getting you ready for surgery. Any new symptoms overnight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2159-07-30 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I slept okay. Just a little anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2159-07-30 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely normal. The surgery should take about an hour. We’ll remove all the non-healing tissue and place the VAC. I’ll see you when you wake up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2159-07-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back in your room. The surgery went very well. We cleaned out the stump and the VAC is working. No complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2159-07-30 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. It feels different already—tighter, but not painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2159-07-30 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the VAC pulling gently. We’ll keep you on IV pain meds for now and switch to oral later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2159-07-30 14:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin? When can I restart that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2159-07-30 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR dropped to 2.0 this morning, so we’ve restarted warfarin at a low dose. But since it takes days to work, we’re also starting a heparin drip to protect your heart valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2159-07-31 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs look stable. The heparin drip is keeping your clotting in check while the warfarin kicks in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2159-07-31 07:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the heparin safe with my dialysis tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2159-07-31 07:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll coordinate the timing. We may pause it briefly during dialysis to reduce bleeding risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2159-07-31 07:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the VAC? Does it need changing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2159-07-31 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We changed it this morning. There was a small clot in the tubing, so we cleared it and reapplied. The wound looks clean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2159-08-01 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had dialysis last night—1.5 liters removed. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2159-08-01 06:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit nauseous afterward, but the Zofran helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2159-08-01 06:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Nausea after dialysis is common. We’ll keep the Zofran available."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2159-08-01 06:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My left heel ulcer—has anyone looked at that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2159-08-01 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the team noted the eschar on your heel. We’re not planning surgery there now, but we’ll keep it clean and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2159-08-02 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We took the VAC off this morning to check the wound. There’s good pink tissue growing—granulation tissue. That’s a great sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2159-08-02 07:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful to hear. Does that mean it’s healing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2159-08-02 07:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s on the right track. We re-applied the VAC. You’re also doing well on pain—we’re switching you to oral meds only."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2159-08-02 07:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can manage the pain. I’d rather not be on too many narcotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2159-08-02 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help you taper back to your baseline OxyContin as you improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2159-08-03 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.2—still a bit low. So we’re keeping the heparin drip going for another day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2159-08-03 06:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of the warfarin dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2159-08-03 06:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We increased it yesterday. It just takes time. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2159-08-03 06:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the spots on my fingers? The dermatology doctor said they’re not calciphylaxis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2159-08-03 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. Dermatology reviewed them and doesn’t think they’re calciphylaxis. We’ll keep an eye on them, but no treatment change needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Big news—your INR is 5.1 now. That’s higher than we want."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means you’re at higher risk for bleeding. So we’ll stop the heparin and hold your warfarin tonight. You won’t take it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. When do I start again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR will be checked tomorrow morning at dialysis. Your PCP will decide the next dose based on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the VAC?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We switched to your home VAC unit today. The visiting nurses will change it every two to three days after you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They’ll come to my house?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2159-08-04 05:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’re already set up. You’ll follow up with Dr. ___ in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re stable, and we’re ready to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your regular meds except warfarin tonight—do not take it. The nurse will draw your INR at home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have dialysis as usual, and they’ll check your INR then. Your PCP’s covering doctor will contact you with the next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have extra hydrocodone for breakthrough pain. But try to taper back to your OxyContin as the pain improves."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The nurses will help you get ready to go home. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I watch for signs of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. If the wound becomes red, swollen, warm, or starts draining more, or if you develop a fever, call your doctor right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And no driving, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not until your surgeon clears you. And use your wheelchair or walker—don’t put weight on the right side."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not planned. If the wound continues to heal, you’ll just need follow-up visits and VAC changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you have all your prescriptions and instructions before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I want to get this recovery on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing exactly that. We’re all rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2159-08-05 08:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. See you at your follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2159-07-29 12:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2159-08-05 15:07:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of mechanical aortic valve replacement, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, coronary artery disease, and prior right below-knee amputation was admitted for a poorly healing amputation stump with eschar. She underwent surgical debridement of the stump and VAC placement. Her INR was elevated at admission (4.3), so warfarin was held. Postoperatively, warfarin was restarted and a heparin drip was used for bridging. The VAC was changed multiple times, with good granulation tissue noted on exam. She received dialysis during the admission, with associated transient nausea managed with ondansetron. Her INR rose to 5.1 by discharge, prompting instructions to hold warfarin and follow up for INR monitoring. She was discharged home with visiting nurse support for VAC care and close outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Other amputation stump complication",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Atherosclerosis of native arteries of the extremities with gangrene",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Ulcer of other part of foot",
      "Renal dialysis status"
    ]
  }
}
